{"step_index":9280,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T06:32:54Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-26T06:32:54Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-26T06:32:54Z\nFile Path: `file:///home/azureuser/.webterminal/media/media_1790404360504_2788.md`\nTotal Lines: 132\nTotal Bytes: 7558\nShowing lines 1 to 132\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # PARENT DIRECTORY LOCK SPECIFICATION & ARCHITECTURAL COMPARISON\n2: \n3: Target Directory: `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER`\n4: Target Host: Azure VM `FatehAli`\n5: Status: DRAFT / ARCHITECTURAL ANALYSIS (NO ACTIONS EXECUTED)\n6: \n7: CHANGE LOG (fixed from previous draft):\n8: - CORRECTED a claim in the original Option B analysis: setting `+i` on\n9:   `AGY-MASTER` itself does NOT selectively allow writes only to files, while\n10:   blocking directory rename. In ext4, `+i` on a directory blocks ALL new\n11:   directory-entry operations inside it — creating, deleting, or renaming\n12:   any file or subdirectory directly under it. Existing subdirectories that\n13:   do NOT themselves have `+i` remain writable **inside themselves** (you can\n14:   still edit a file's contents inside `TASKS/active/`), but you cannot add or\n15:   remove entries in `AGY-MASTER/` itself once you've locked it.\n16: - This means: every subdirectory AGY needs to write NEW files into (queue\n17:   folders, logs, reports) MUST be created BEFORE `chattr +i` is applied to\n18:   the parent, and none of those specific subdirectories should themselves\n19:   get `+i` (only the parent + selected top-level files should).\n20: - Execution order across drafts 02 and 03 has been made explicit — see\n21:   Section 4.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 1. THE PROBLEM: EXT4 DIRECTORY RENAMING VULNERABILITY\n26: \n27: In Linux (POSIX / ext4), the permission to rename or delete a directory\n28: depends on the write permission of its **PARENT directory**, not the\n29: directory itself.\n30: \n31: - Current Parent Directory: `/home/azureuser` (\n<truncated 4548 bytes>\nKS/{queue,active,completed}\n96: mkdir -p /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/INCIDENTS/{active,resolved}\n97: mkdir -p /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/ACTIONS/{pending,approved,history}\n98: mkdir -p /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS/daily\n99: mkdir -p /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS\n100: chown -R azureuser:azureuser \\\n101:     /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/TASKS \\\n102:     /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/INCIDENTS \\\n103:     /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/ACTIONS \\\n104:     /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS \\\n105:     /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS\n106: \n107: # STEP 2 — Lock top-level canonical architecture files individually\n108: sudo chattr +i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/AGENTS.md\n109: sudo chattr +i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/PROJECT_REGISTRY.md\n110: sudo chattr +i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/safety_levels.json\n111: sudo chattr +i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/protected_registry.json\n112: \n113: # STEP 3 — LAST: lock the AGY-MASTER directory itself.\n114: # Run this only after Steps 1 and 2 are fully verified complete — once this\n115: # runs, no new file or subdirectory can be added directly under AGY-MASTER\n116: # (existing subdirectories from Step 1 remain writable inside themselves).\n117: sudo chattr +i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER\n118: ```\n119: \n120: ### Rollback Procedure (If Maintenance Required):\n121: This MUST be run by a human with direct console/SSH access — it is not\n122: available to azureuser via sudo once draft 01 is applied, by design. It\n123: requires either temporarily re-adding a scoped `chattr` sudo rule, or logging\n124: in as root directly via Azure Serial Console.\n125: ```bash\n126: sudo chattr -i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER\n127: sudo chattr -i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/AGENTS.md\n128: sudo chattr -i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/PROJECT_REGISTRY.md\n129: sudo chattr -i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/safety_levels.json\n130: sudo chattr -i /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/protected_registry.json\n131: ```\n132: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
