{"step_index":9282,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T06:32:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-26T06:32:58Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-26T06:32:58Z\nFile Path: `file:///home/azureuser/.webterminal/media/media_1790404361408_2790.md`\nTotal Lines: 171\nTotal Bytes: 6734\nShowing lines 1 to 171\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # EXTERNAL IMMUTABLE BACKUP ARCHITECTURE (WORM & REMOTE GIT)\n2: \n3: Target Host: Azure VM `FatehAli`\n4: Status: DRAFT SPECIFICATION (NO ACTIONS EXECUTED)\n5: \n6: CHANGE LOG (fixed from previous draft):\n7: - FLAGGED: the git backup script's `git push origin main` line was commented\n8:   out in the original draft. As written, that script only commits locally —\n9:   if the VM disk is destroyed, that local git history is destroyed with it,\n10:   which defeats the entire purpose of an \"external\" backup. Section 3 below\n11:   now requires setting up a deploy key BEFORE uncommenting the push line, and\n12:   the script has a safety check that warns (rather than silently no-oping) if\n13:   no push remote is reachable.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 1. WHY EXTERNAL IMMUTABLE BACKUP IS MANDATORY\n18: \n19: Even with strict sudoers and `chattr +i`, an attacker with physical/hypervisor\n20: access, a kernel exploit, or a disk failure could still destroy local data.\n21: The only defense that survives total VM compromise is **storage outside the\n22: VM**:\n23: - The VM has **zero Azure credentials** and **no Managed Identity**.\n24: - Data stored in an Azure Blob Storage container with **Immutable Blob\n25:   Storage (WORM — Write Once, Read Many)** cannot be deleted or overwritten\n26:   by any process inside the VM, because the VM has no credential path to\n27:   Azure Resource Manager at all.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: ## 2. AZURE BLOB WORM POLICY SETUP (EXECUTE FROM AZURE CLOUD SHELL)\n32: \n33: > 🛑 **CRITICAL OPERATIONAL REQUIREMENT:**\n34: > These Azure CLI commands **CANNOT** and **MUST NOT*\n<truncated 3919 bytes>\n123: \n124: TIMESTAMP=$(date -u +\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n125: FAILURES=0\n126: \n127: for repo in \"${BACKUP_REPOS[@]}\"; do\n128:     if [[ -d \"$repo/.git\" ]]; then\n129:         echo \"[+] Syncing repository: $repo at $TIMESTAMP\"\n130:         cd \"$repo\"\n131: \n132:         # Confirm a push remote is actually configured before relying on this\n133:         if ! git remote get-url origin >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n134:             echo \"[!] WARNING: $repo has no 'origin' remote configured — commits will stay LOCAL ONLY. This defeats the purpose of external backup.\"\n135:             FAILURES=$((FAILURES + 1))\n136:             continue\n137:         fi\n138: \n139:         git add -A\n140:         if ! git diff-index --quiet HEAD --; then\n141:             git commit -m \"Automated DR Snapshot: $TIMESTAMP\"\n142:         fi\n143: \n144:         # Push is now active (not commented out) — but only reaches here if\n145:         # the prerequisite deploy-key setup above has been completed and\n146:         # tested manually at least once.\n147:         if ! git push origin main; then\n148:             echo \"[!] WARNING: push failed for $repo — check deploy key / network\"\n149:             FAILURES=$((FAILURES + 1))\n150:         fi\n151:     else\n152:         echo \"[-] Not a git repo, skipping: $repo\"\n153:     fi\n154: done\n155: \n156: if [[ $FAILURES -gt 0 ]]; then\n157:     echo \"[!] $FAILURES repo(s) did not reach the remote this run — investigate before trusting this backup.\"\n158:     exit 1\n159: fi\n160: ```\n161: \n162: ### Crontab Integration (Draft):\n163: ```cron\n164: # Run every night at 02:00 AM UTC\n165: 0 2 * * * /bin/bash /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/git-sync-backup.sh >> /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS/daily/git-backup.log 2>&1\n166: ```\n167: \n168: **Do not enable this cron job until you have manually run the script once,\n169: confirmed it pushes successfully, and confirmed the commit is visible on\n170: GitHub/GitLab from a separate machine.**\n171: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
