{"step_index":9287,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T06:33:06Z","thinking":"The initial file's syntax for restricted commands within the sudoers file was incorrect; tags were concatenated without spaces. Corrected this, ensuring each command set (APT, SYSTEMCTL, DOCKER) is listed on a new line with the proper `NOPASSWD:NOEXEC:` syntax. The objective is to refine the configuration of the commands.\n\n\nExamining the mechanism of `NOEXEC`, its implications for dynamic linking and static binaries were considered to ensure complete restriction. The configuration must disable `90-cloud-init-users` to avoid permission conflicts. A secondary SSH session is recommended for testing.\n\nThe initial locking strategy was flawed. Changing ownership of the master directory doesn't prevent renaming; the parent's permissions control that. The right approach involves locking the master directory after subdirectories are established and top-level files made immutable.\n\n\nRevised the backup script to ensure commits are pushed to the remote repository and included deploy key instructions for SSH access. Documentation clarified the method of data ingestion into the object storage system without VM credentials.\n\nVerification tests are enhanced: exit codes are now the primary check; a dedicated test uses a syscall to probe restrictions directly, and checks confirm the `i` attribute for immutability. Included a sanity check to verify subdirectory writability even after locking the parent. An IMDS token test was added to check access.\n\n\nThe peer-reviewed files include comprehensive tests and corrections for edge cases, addressing ordering issues and replacing weak assertions with robust tests. The backup script has been improved to ensure proper external pushing, and sudoers syntax is corrected for `NOEXEC` chaining. The immutability order of execution is clarified. Verification confirms the improvements should be synchronized with the local drafts.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# ==============================================================================\\n# /etc/sudoers.d/99-azureuser-restricted (DRAFT ONLY)\\n# ==============================================================================\\n# Principle of Least Privilege: Whitelist-only with NOEXEC\\n# Target: Azure VM 'FatehAli' (User: azureuser)\\n# Status: DRAFT - DO NOT DEPLOY WITHOUT EXPLICIT APPROVAL AND BACKUP\\n#\\n# CHANGE LOG (fixed from previous draft):\\n# - FIXED: tag syntax was `NOEXEC: NOPASSWD:` (invalid — space-separated tags\\n#   before the alias list are not parsed the way the old draft assumed).\\n#   Correct sudoers syntax chains tags with colons, no spaces, immediately\\n#   before the command list: NOPASSWD:NOEXEC:\\n#\\n# CRITICAL DEPLOYMENT PREREQUISITE:\\n# 1. The default file '/etc/sudoers.d/90-cloud-init-users' currently grants:\\n#    'azureuser ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL'\\n#    If 90-cloud-init-users remains active, this restricted policy will be\\n#    bypassed because sudo evaluates rules additively and the LAST matching\\n#    rule for a given command wins — but a broad NOPASSWD:ALL earlier in\\n#    evaluation order can still grant access this file tries to deny.\\n#    To activate, 90-cloud-init-users MUST be removed or renamed with a\\n#    lower priority prefix (e.g. 00-) so this file's rules are evaluated after it,\\n#    or simply deleted since NOPASSWD:ALL is being replaced entirely.\\n# 2. Safety Rule: Always keep an active Azure Serial Console session open, or\\n#    take an Azure VM Disk Snapshot before modifying sudoers!\\n# 3. Always validate syntax before installing:\\n#      sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/99-azureuser-restricted\\n#    A non-zero exit code means DO NOT proceed — fix the syntax first.\\n# 4. After installing, open a SECOND ssh session (do not close your current\\n#    one) and test `sudo -l` as azureuser before logging out of the first.\\n#    If sudo is broken, your current session's sudo cache may still work\\n#    long enough to revert via the serial console.\\n# ==============================\n<truncated 3972 bytes>","Description":"\"Update 01-sudoers-restricted.draft with chained NOPASSWD:NOEXEC: tag syntax and refined exclusions\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/01-sudoers-restricted.draft\"","toolAction":"\"Updating 01-sudoers-restricted.draft\"","toolSummary":"\"Sync 01-sudoers-restricted\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
